    {
      "_id": "blz2xxeG1IwVQZDI",
      "name": "Rage",
      "type": "action",
      "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/OneAction.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "folder": null,
      "sort": 0,
      "flags": {
        "core": {}
      },
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You aren't @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.HL2l2VRSaQHu9lUw]{Fatigued} or raging</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong>: <span style=\"font-family: var(--font-primary); font-size: var(--font-size-14);\">@Compendium[pf2e.feat-effects.z3uyCMBddrPK5umr]{Effect: Rage}</span></p>\n<p>You tap into your inner fury and begin raging. You gain a number of temporary Hit Points equal to your level plus your Constitution modifier. This frenzy lasts for 1 minute, until there are no enemies you can perceive, or until you fall @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious}, whichever comes first. You can't voluntarily stop raging. While you are raging:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You deal 2 additional damage with melee weapons and unarmed attacks. This additional damage is halved if your weapon or unarmed attack is agile.</li>\n<li>You take a -1 penalty to AC.</li>\n<li>You can't use actions with the concentrate trait unless they also have the rage trait. You can @Compendium[pf2e.actionspf2e.BlAOM2X92SI6HMtJ]{Seek} while raging.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>After you stop raging, you lose any remaining temporary Hit Points from Rage, and you can't Rage again for 1 minute.</p>"
        },
        "source": {
          "value": "Pathfinder Core Rulebook"
        },
        "traits": {
          "value": [
            "concentrate",
            "barbarian",
